#+TITLE: Native EPURE shutdown leaves save dialogs and output callbacks active
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: native Windows CAD qualification
#+BRANCH: codex/fermeture-cao-20261023

* Reproduction
Run installed SCHME or SCHMS under ALFE on AutoCAD 2022 or BricsCAD V25
with EPURE. Successful assertions can be followed by a Dessin1 save dialog,
a forced BricsCAD termination, or an AutoCAD callback error during shutdown.

* Findings and corrections under qualification
- Keep native printers until the entire protocol server loop and its final
  logging finish, then restore them. Restoring at C:MAIN return is too early.
- Close AutoCAD documents without saving, wait for quiescence and retry
  transient COM rejections. Never Quit after a failed document close.
- Send BricsCAD QUIT and its discard answer from AutoLISP command rather
  than as separate SCR tokens; allow bounded natural exit before fallback.

* Evidence (2026-10-23)
34 targeted checks pass on both SBCL and CCL, including ownership, bridge generation,
protocol restoration ordering and bounded process shutdown. Windows cscript
mocks show retry success and refusal to Quit after permanent close failure.
SCHMS on pb: 3 assertions pass and BricsCAD exits naturally with code 0
using the isolated qualification plugin. Further native account/project
qualification is still pending; no full-matrix success is claimed.

* Additional lifecycle finding
On this Windows host, GetExitCodeProcess can return 47806 and .NET
Process.HasExited can be true while WaitForSingleObject(handle, 0) returns
WAIT_TIMEOUT and Restart Manager still lists the process as a DLL owner.
Native qualification must use the process handle signal, not only the
reported exit code. The operational collector now has that stronger test.
